# Family Sharing Baseline

Do not treat family-sharing / household changes as complete until
`docs/Family Sharing Regression Checklist.md` has been run (or explicitly
scheduled with the user). Contracts live in `docs/family-sharing-baseline.md`.

When changing household APIs, verify **both** localhost Express
(`server/routes/households.js`) and Vercel **explicit** entries under
`api/households/` (`current.js`, `index.js`, etc.). Do **not** use
`[...route]` catch-all on this non-Next Vercel project. Localhost success alone
is not enough. Keep routing/responses in `server/lib/household-api-handler.js`
and run `node scripts/test-household-api-contract.mjs`. After deploy, confirm
production via `X-Household-Handler` / `X-Deploy-Commit` headers.

Hard rules:

- Do not return `status: deleted` households from `GET /api/households/current`
- Do not hardcode UID/householdId to force `activeHouseholdId`
- Do not auto-create households in current/discovery
- Do not raise/remove `create:user` rate limits to mask duplicate creates
- remove/leave must soft-deactivate members; keep household `active` for remaining members
- Do not physically delete shared or personal pantry data in remove/leave/migrate

Smoke guide: `scripts/family-sharing-smoke-test.md`
Project rule copy: `CLAUDE.md`
